+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>Evidence & open questions · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/atlas-hierarchy-v0.2.css"><script src="/assets/atlas-hierarchy-v0.2.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="editorial"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/"><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/"><span>02</span>Foundations</a><a href="/research/"><span>03</span>Research programmes</a><a href="/evidence/" aria-current="page"><span>04</span>Evidence & open questions</a><a href="/papers/"><span>05</span>Papers & reading</a><a href="/archive/"><span>06</span>Research archive</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><div class="atlas-utilities"><a href="/updates/">Updates</a><a href="/sources/">Search sources</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribute</a></div><span class="status-dot"></span>Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>AI-assisted research<br>Review remains scope-specific</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 Chicago · PFX v0.1</div><h1>A conditional clock overlap for the diamond prefix.</h1><p class="lede">A proved local preparation box reduces the controller sensitivity enough to admit a fast SAR and LC component route mathematically.</p></div>
+<aside class="callout"><strong>Derived conditional · Clock interval passes · Hardware HOLD · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>The five-page theorem proves local derivative and state-barrier bounds. Exact symbolic checks and twelve arithmetic controls pass. Supplier catalogue values do not establish operating-band accuracy, noise tails or actuator response; independent review remains pending.</p></aside>
+<div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/prefix-feasibility-v0.1/UD_PREFIX_FEASIBILITY_THEOREM_v0.1.pdf">Read five-page theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/prefix-feasibility-v0.1/UD_PREFIX_FEASIBILITY_THEOREM_v0.1_RELEASE.zip">Download source package ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/prefix-feasibility-v0.1/COMPONENT_ROUTE_v0.1.json">Open component route and identification gates</a></div>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>The preparation gives a tighter region to prove.</h2><p>Near the specified CD-1 initial state, lifted angles stay within 1/100; electric and imaginary matter coordinates within 1/50; real matter coordinates lie between 2/3 and 3/4. Exact Hamiltonian majorants give target Lipschitz bound 4, actual speed bound 8/5 and Gauss bound 4.</p><p>A joint state/reconstruction and actuator-tracking barrier keeps nominal and both fault laws within this box through the short decision window. This is a proof on the specified prefix, not a sampled-trajectory assumption or a full-horizon replacement.</p></div></section>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>The physical clock interval is nonempty.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Proposed quantity</th><th>Conditional requirement</th></tr></thead><tbody>
+<tr><td>Clock interval</td><td>8/575 &lt; t₀ ≤ 1/48 seconds</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Example physical clock</td><td>t₀=1/60 second</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Command period; additional true latency</td><td>1 μs; at most 2 μs</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Identified actuator time constant</td><td>At most 1 μs</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Input error; complete command error</td><td>3/100000; 1/25000</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Total residual; slack below 1/100</td><td>481/50000=0.00962; 19/50000</td></tr>
+</tbody></table><p>The plant model now retains series resistance and actively cancels it. The operating-band premises are L≥0.85 H, C≥0.8 mF and R≤6.6125 Ω on every canonical pair. Under balanced common-action scales these imply λ&lt;48t₀. Actual component calibration must substantiate those premises.</p></div></section>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>A specific component route can now be screened.</h2><p>The candidate route uses Hammond 193S chokes, Nichicon UES1C102MHM bipolar capacitors, AD4630-24 acquisition and AD5791 command converters. Manufacturer sources and exact conditions are linked in the manuscript and machine-readable record.</p><p>Acquisition is proposed at 2 MSPS; commands update at 1 MHz. The DAC serial frame does not fit fresh 2 MHz writes. A complete parallel transfer, evaluation and command-latching design must close the proposed latency. Independent coupling, actuator and work readout remain required.</p><p>The two fault-detection slacks improve to about 0.00624634 and 0.00704346. A ten-time-constant preload bounds release tracking by 33/40000, provided the specified hold-history and distortion premises hold.</p></div></section>
+<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Clock overlap is not hardware admission.</h2><p>The capacitor’s published rated-voltage leakage limit does not certify the much smaller current-residual allowance at the proposed test voltage. Measure the actual charge/voltage relation, leakage or bounded compensation, ESR and dielectric memory. Measure the choke’s flux/current law and hysteresis at operating bias.</p><p>A conditional noise-family bound is supplied for at most 10000 controller-coordinate errors, given explicit sub-Gaussian tails. Supplier RMS or SNR does not establish that premise. Calibration, witnesses, endpoints and clocks need separate joint uncertainty allocation.</p><p>The next return must close operating-band plant identification, full timing, input and command errors, actuator response, startup and independent sensing. No purchases or experiments have occurred. Hardware remains HOLD; no full CD-1 campaign or SDW admission is asserted.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/clock-plant/">Read the earlier clock–plant compatibility theorem →</a></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public atlas</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
