rapping-v01"><div class="eyebrow">16 October 2026 UTC · Theorem milestone 0.1</div><h2>Nonlinear trapping now tolerates a declared model-error budget</h2><p>A sufficient static Hamiltonian-gradient budget gives all-time trapping around a selected nominal balanced orbit and a nearby compact minimizing invariant set. Time-dependent errors receive a cumulative variation condition, and a separate external-forcing contract limits injected work. An exact resonant oscillator shows why instantaneous smallness alone cannot support a general all-time guarantee.</p><p>The theorem translates kinetic, diamond, hopping and site-detuning errors into one gradient cap. It also bounds each complex loop readout error by 21η and supplies a split state/instrument noise reserve for real and oriented classifiers. All 30 new exact/symbolic checks and six synthetic matrix-gradient/readout fixtures passed; the prior interval certificate remains a dependency, not a new count. No experimental data or physical detector map is supplied. The nominal orbit need not remain invariant, and no unique displaced branch is proved. Development, no registry entry; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#robust-trapping-v01">Read the model-robustness theorem →</a></article><article class="claim" id="energy-barrier-v01"><div class="eyebrow">16 October 2026 UTC · Theorem milestone 0.1</div><h2>A quantitative nonlinear trapping budget is certified</h2><p>The six balanced finite-offset phase branches now have an explicit outer trapping radius, boundary energy barrier and smaller sufficient initial ball at every finite rank. The proof certifies the slow scalar Hessian floor and bounds global second and third geodesic energy derivatives. It uses distance to the compact gauge/species-phase orbit and preserves the residual stabilizer constraint.</p><p>All 211 exact/rigorous interval checks passed across 64 new parameter cells. Six synthetic jet diagnostics passed; no