 existence now has a numerical validity region</h2><p>A regularized full stationary system certifies the 26 phase branches on 0&lt;ε≤10⁻⁵. The certificate covers the rescaled zero endpoint, all scalar Morse indices and explicit amplitude and loop-readout errors. It also gives sufficient deterministic noise budgets for both oriented phases and six labeled real loop amplitudes.</p><p>Exact symmetry sectors and scaled Schur complements bound the stable soft-mode frequency ratio to within 0.005 of its limiting value when a=N=r=1. The proof replay passed 1,536 nested interval boxes and 2,048 spectral cut tests. The interval is sufficient, not maximal; uniqueness is within the certified tubes. Higher-rank stationary embeddings are covered, while their full normal stability radius remains open. No experimental data are analyzed. Development, no registry entry; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#finite-offset-v01">Read the finite-offset theorem →</a></article><article class="claim" id="branch-readout-v01"><div class="eyebrow">15 October 2026 UTC · Theorem milestone 0.1</div><h2>Branch observables and a bounded-error measurement design</h2><p>A matter-dressed Wilson observable is invariant under the full local U(r) gauge group. On the one-active-color branch embeddings its oriented phases recover the critical vector exactly, because the nonlinear fast correction cancels. Fourth-moment fingerprints distinguish the three families and a signed cubic separates the two body-diagonal permutation orbits.</p><p>The theorem proves a sufficient phase-noise margin and an exact information limit for real-only channels. A proposed measurement contract specifies phase, Gauss, calibration and small-response requirements. Two primary studies offer gauge or holonomy readout precedents; their different actions and geometries do not currently provide a direct UD branch test. This is a limited compatibility screen, with no empirical reanalysis. The frozen action and ledger are unchanged; independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#branch-readout-v01">Read the branch-readout theorem →</a></article><article class="claim" id="critical-bifurcation-v01"><div class="eyebrow">15 October 2026 UTC · Theorem milestone 0.1</div><h2>New stable phase equilibria appear beyond the curved-orbit threshold</h2><p>The exact stationary energy yields six balanced minima, twelve index-one saddles and eight index-two saddles for sufficiently small positive coefficient excess. These counts retain vertex labels and describe phase-amplitude patterns on the fixed carrier. The scalar local diagram is complete; the higher-rank theorem concerns embeddings of these branches.</p><p>A reversing symmetry supplies the exact scalar instability counts and leading soft frequencies, including Gauss backreaction. The balanced branches persist as full-rank stable orbits near threshold, while the original orbit remains unstable above its previous boundary. Energy conservation rules out attraction to the minima; a sourced preparation or selection law remains open. 66 exact constructor checks and twelve full stationary-energy solutions with 42-pair spectra passed. No numerical bound on the theorem's neighborhood radius or new dynamical trajectory is claimed. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#critical-bifurcation-v01">Read the bifurcation theorem →</a></article><article class="claim" id="residual-gauss-v01"><div class="eyebrow">15 October 2026 UTC · Theorem milestone 0.1</div><h2>The final residual Gauss constraint is explicit</h2><p>The extra-color oscillator list now has its admissibility rule: opposite oscillator orientations must balance in total amplitude, and the full matrix charge must cancel with the unused vacuum commutators. A weighted-shift construction completes every trace-balanced color state with one vacuum oscillator, with an energy